# .dockerignore — build-context filter for `COPY . .` in Dockerfile
#
# Second line of defence. .rsync-exclude keeps private workspace files off the
# droplet in the first place; this keeps them out of the image layers even if
# something lands in /opt/praetorium by another route (manual scp, a restored
# backup, leftovers from an older deploy).
#
# There was no .dockerignore before 2026-09-16, which is why MEMORY.md, USER.md,
# SOUL.md and 172 memory/ files were baked into praetorium-app:latest.
#
# Deliberately a blacklist, unlike .rsync-exclude: an over-tight allowlist here
# would break the build instead of failing loudly, and the rsync filter is
# already the primary control.
#
# ORDERING MATTERS AND IS THE OPPOSITE OF RSYNC: Docker evaluates every line and
# the LAST match wins. The re-includes at the bottom therefore override every
# pattern above them. That is load-bearing — the app legitimately serves PDFs
# from app/static/tradoc/ and app/static/maps/training-sites/, so the `!app/`
# rule guarantees a document glob can never strip real application assets,
# regardless of how Docker scopes `*` against path separators.

# secrets and VCS
.env
.env.*
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
.github

# agent workspace / private notes
MEMORY.md
USER.md
SOUL.md
IDENTITY.md
AGENTS.md
HEARTBEAT.md
DREAMS.md
UNIT_CONTEXT.md
TOOLS.md
memory/
.openclaw/
skills/
references/
prompts.json
exec-approvals.json

# scratch and personal documents sitting in the repo root
tmp/
tmp_*
archive/
projects/
area-studies/
recipe-work/
recon-images/
html-reports/
audit-*/
*.pdf
*.csv
*.CSV
*.pptx
*.webp
*.log

# build/test caches
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.bak*

# --- re-includes: never let the rules above touch shipped application code ---
# Last match wins, so these are final. Keep this block at the bottom.
!app/
!tests/
!migrations/
!scripts/
!config.py
!alembic.ini
!leave_return_runner.py
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
!pyproject.toml
